Generic single-database configuration.

NOTHING RUNS THESE AUTOMATICALLY. Read this before assuming a deploy applied them.

`azure-pipelines.yml` at the repo root builds the FRONTEND image and hands off to
ArgoCD via a manifest bump. It never touches the database, and its own header says the
backend has no pipeline yet. There is therefore no step, anywhere, that runs

    alembic upgrade head

against a deployed environment. Every migration in `versions/` reaches a database only
because a person ran it there.

WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN IT SOUNDS. An unapplied migration does not announce itself.
The ones in this directory are mostly indexes and grants, and a missing index is a
slow page rather than an error — `0061_audit_tenant_created_index` and
`0062_audit_search_indexes` both fall into that category, and an environment without
them serves the Audit Trail from sequential scans while looking perfectly healthy.
`0005_audit_append_only` is worse: without it the app role keeps UPDATE and DELETE on
`audit_events`, so the append-only guarantee the product claims is simply absent, and
nothing fails to tell you.

WHEN THE BACKEND GETS A PIPELINE, the upgrade belongs in it, ahead of the rollout and
as its own step — not at application startup, where N replicas racing the same
migration is its own failure mode.

UNTIL THEN, per environment, after every deploy that includes a new file in
`versions/`:

    cd backend && alembic upgrade head

`alembic current` says where an environment actually is; compare it against the newest
file in `versions/` rather than assuming.
